#: inc/admin-settings-page.php:1871
#: inc/breadcrumb-auto-emit.php:375
#: inc/breadcrumb-auto-emit.php:420
msgid "Breadcrumbs"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings-page.php:1161
msgid "Links in the breadcrumb trail."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings-page.php:1164
#: inc/admin-settings-page.php:1841
msgid "Footer"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings-page.php:1165
msgid "Links in the footer."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings-page.php:1170
msgid "AWT underlines links, so a link is never marked out by colour alone. Carbon leaves links without an underline and brings it back only when you point at one."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings-page.php:1175
#: inc/admin-settings-page.php:1275
#: inc/admin-settings-page.php:1436
#: inc/admin-settings-page.php:1874
msgid "Accessibility benefit"
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: opening <a> tag to WCAG 1.4.1; 2: closing </a> tag
#: inc/admin-settings-page.php:1180
#, php-format
msgid "Colour on its own may carry a link only when the link is clearly different from the text around it — at least three times the contrast, under the %1$sWCAG \"Use of Color\" guideline (1.4.1, Level A)%2$s. Carbon's blue reaches 3.62 to 1 against body text in light mode, but only 2.14 to 1 in dark mode, so in dark mode colour alone is not enough. Change your colours and the light figure can drop below the line too. An underline settles it either way."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings-page.php:1190
msgid "Underline links"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings-page.php:1194
msgid "Underline links across the whole site."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings-page.php:1197
msgid "Turn this off to use Carbon's link style everywhere, where colour marks a link and the underline appears only when you point at it. The choices below stay saved, and come back when you turn this on again."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings-page.php:1206
msgid "Nothing is underlined right now, because the switch above is off. The choices below are saved and will apply as soon as you turn it back on."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings-page.php:1213
msgid "Where to underline"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings-page.php:1216
msgid "One switch per place a link appears, because the reason differs: a link in a paragraph has to stand out from the text around it, while a menu item is found by where it sits."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings-page.php:1241
msgid "Never underlined, whatever you choose here: buttons, pagination numbers, tags and cards. Each of those is already marked out by its own shape, so an underline would read as emphasis instead. Plain links you type into your text are left alone too — they keep the underline your browser already gives them, whichever way you set these switches."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings-page.php:1270
msgid "When someone moves through your page with the Tab key, the control they land on is marked so they can see where they are. This sets how that mark is drawn on buttons."
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: opening <a> tag to WCAG 2.4.7; 2: closing </a> tag; 3: opening <a> tag to WCAG 2.4.13; 4: closing </a> tag
#: inc/admin-settings-page.php:1280
#, php-format
msgid "A focused control has to be visible, under the %1$sWCAG \"Focus Visible\" guideline (2.4.7, Level AA)%2$s. How big the mark has to be is set by %3$s\"Focus Appearance\" (2.4.13, Level AAA)%4$s: at least as much area as a 2-pixel line around the control, and a clear change from how that same spot looks unfocused. AWT meets both whichever way you set this. What changes is how easy it is to check. Carbon builds a button's mark out of a border and two shadows, so there is no single thickness to read and anyone auditing your site has to work it out from three overlapping layers. One outline answers the question directly."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings-page.php:1292
msgid "Button focus outline"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings-page.php:1296
msgid "Mark a focused button with one outline, just outside its edge."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings-page.php:1299
msgid "Turn this off to use Carbon's look instead: two rings of different thickness, drawn inside the button's edge. Both are easy to see, and both meet the guidelines. The single outline is simply easier to measure and to explain."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings-page.php:1308
msgid "Buttons are using Carbon's two-ring style right now. This still meets the guidelines — it is a look, not a step down."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings-page.php:1314
msgid "This switch covers buttons only. Links, form fields, menus, tabs and everything else keep the outline they already have, whichever way you set it. Buttons were the one place the mark was built out of layers instead of drawn as a single line."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings-page.php:1336
msgid "Compact (0.875×)"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings-page.php:1337
msgid "Slightly smaller than the browser default. Best when fitting more on screen matters more than easy reading."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings-page.php:1340
msgid "Default (1.0×)"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings-page.php:1341
msgid "The standard type scale. Recommended for most sites."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings-page.php:1344
msgid "Comfortable (1.125×)"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings-page.php:1345
msgid "Slightly larger. Recommended for sites with older audiences or low-vision readers."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings-page.php:1350
msgid "Resize every font on your site by the same amount. Heading-to-body proportions and line spacing stay balanced at any size."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings-page.php:1353
msgid "AWT uses IBM Plex Sans for text and IBM Plex Mono for code, chosen for on-screen readability. You can't swap fonts yet, because many web fonts are harder to read."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings-page.php:1357
#: inc/admin-settings-page.php:1360
msgid "Size scale"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings-page.php:1391
msgid "Preview"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings-page.php:1392
msgid "Updates live as you change the size scale. Save changes to apply across the site."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings-page.php:1394
msgid "Heading 1 — Productive heading 06"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings-page.php:1395
msgid "Heading 2 — Productive heading 04"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings-page.php:1396
msgid "Heading 3 — Productive heading 03"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings-page.php:1398
msgid "Body text. The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog. 1234567890. AWT resizes every font by the same amount, so spacing stays balanced at any size. Compact fits more on screen; Comfortable gives larger, easier-to-read type."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings-page.php:1429
msgid "Text around form fields"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings-page.php:1431
msgid "Every field on a form carries a label, sometimes a hint, and a message when something is wrong. Carbon sets all three smaller than your body text. This puts them at the same size as everything else."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings-page.php:1438
msgid "These three strings are the ones a person has to read in order to fill your form in, and at Carbon's size they are the smallest text on the page. No accessibility rule sets a minimum text size, so both settings pass. Bigger text is simply easier to read, and it matters most where reading it is the only way through."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings-page.php:1444
msgid "Form text size"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings-page.php:1455
msgid "Show labels, hints and error messages at body text size."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings-page.php:1458
msgid "Turn this off to use Carbon's sizes instead, where this text is a step smaller than your body text."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings-page.php:1467
msgid "Form labels, hints and error messages are using Carbon's smaller size right now. This still meets the guidelines — it is a size, not a step down."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings-page.php:1473
msgid "One field style is left out on purpose: the one that floats its label inside the box. There, the label sits in a slot built for smaller text, so growing it would crowd what the visitor types."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: link to Site Editor
#: inc/admin-settings-page.php:1541
#, php-format
msgid "Edit colors in %s. Custom colors you add there appear in this audit alongside Carbon's defaults."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings-page.php:1542
msgid "Site Editor → Styles → Colors"
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings-page.php:1547
msgid "This check tests each color only against the backgrounds it's meant to appear on, using the WCAG contrast level its role requires: 4.5:1 for body and link text, 3:1 for interface parts like button edges, icons, focus rings, and borders. Color pairings a color isn't meant for aren't shown."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin-settings-page.php:1582
msgid "No palette colors found."
msgstr ""

